Here is the complete solution for analyzing the truck array:

```java
public static void analyzeTrucks(Truck[] trucks) {
    if (trucks.length == 0) return;
    Truck highest = trucks[0];
    double maxMileage = trucks[0].getDistanceTravelled() / trucks[0].getFuelConsumed();
    int excellent = 0, good = 0, average = 0, poor = 0;
    double totalMileage = 0;

    for (Truck t : trucks) {
        double mileage = t.getDistanceTravelled() / t.getFuelConsumed();
        totalMileage += mileage;
        if (mileage >= 18) excellent++;
        else if (mileage >= 15) good++;
        else if (mileage >= 10) average++;
        else poor++;

        if (mileage > maxMileage) {
            maxMileage = mileage;
            highest = t;
        }
    }
    System.out.println("Highest Mileage Truck ID: " + highest.getTruckId());
